From 750126a6fb7aae3ea80c176496f2070ce44ec0b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:12:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the tasks card sits below the pinned user message

Zeo 0.10.2, from the operator's session on 0.10.1. The tasks card's
free area is the conversation's viewport (0037, 0088), and 0102's
pinned user message floats over the top of that same viewport, so in
its top corners the card was drawn over the header.

What floats over the top of the conversation now says where it ends:
ThreadView::top_overlay_bottom, a cell the overlay writes at prepaint
from its own bounds -- its height is only known there: minimized,
expanded, or wrapped at the panel's width -- and render clears before
the overlay is built again, so a header that is gone leaves nothing
behind. The panel's free-area closure runs in the card's deferred
prepaint, after the thread's, and takes that strip off the top through
tasks_card::below_top_overlay, clamped to the area so a stray value
can never move the card over the toolbar or the editor.

The mechanism is not the pinned message's: any later overlay at the
top of a conversation -- the operator named a sub-thread's bar -- sets
the same cell.

Tests: tasks_card::placement (the free area starts below an overlay at
its top; an overlay outside the area never moves it out). Seen failing
with the clamp replaced by a plain minimum.
---

diff --git a/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs b/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs
index c73a080..d0ba7e9 100644
--- a/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs
+++ b/crates/agent_ui/src/agent_panel.rs
@@ -5040,7 +5040,11 @@ impl AgentPanel {
                 // header bars and the callouts and editor stacked under it.
                 let viewport = thread_view.list_state.viewport_bounds();
                 if !viewport.is_empty() {
-                    return viewport;
+                    // Minus whatever floats over the viewport's top in this frame.
+                    return crate::tasks_card::below_top_overlay(
+                        viewport,
+                        thread_view.top_overlay_bottom.get(),
+                    );
                 }
             } else if let Some(editor) = thread_view
                 .message_editor
